  "context": "2026-11-07 delivered in PR #4036 (merge commit 1c1651e7a66131d768ac1c8c9de10b2920bd6f0d). Source of NaN: BenchBox's ClickHouseLocalClient.execute converted the Arrow result with .to_pandas(), which turns NULL floats into NaN (and NULL ints into floats); chDB's Arrow bytes already carry a true NULL. Minimal reproduction: pa.ipc stream of chdb.connect().query(\"SELECT CAST(NULL AS Nullable(Float64)) AS x\", format=\"ArrowStream\"): table.to_pylist() -> [{'x': None}] but table.to_pandas() rows -> [(nan,)] (/tmp/rv/chdbnan-repro.py). Fix: rows are built directly from the Arrow columns, no pandas. Parity over the 22 TPC-H SF0.01 queries: before fix 21/22 (Q17 046af8ff vs dfe6161f); after fix 22/22 on chDB 3.7.2 (macOS arm64, /tmp/rv/chdbnan-parity-after.log) and on the locked chDB 4.1.6 / chdb-core 26.1.0 on Linux aarch64 in an Apple container (/tmp/rv/chdbnan-linux-4x.log). Default: ClickHouse local mode now defaults fetch_mode to arrow (server and cloud stay rows). Review fix kept row building inside the timed interval.",
  "description": "Found in the Arrow fetch work (#4012) on chDB 3.7.2. Rows-against-Arrow digest parity over the 22 TPC-H SF0.01 queries matched 21 of 22. Q17 returns NaN on the rows path and NULL on the Arrow path. Arrow therefore stays opt-in for ClickHouse local mode. The locked chDB 4.1.6 wheel does not load on this macOS, so the parity run used 3.7.2 (see chdb-4x-engine-load-verification-20261006).\n\nOne of the two paths misrepresents an empty-aggregate result. That affects result digests and validation for chDB in rows mode, which is the current default.\n\nChange. Determine the SQL-correct value for Q17's output on that data (NULL for AVG over an empty set) and where NaN is introduced: the chDB driver, BenchBox's row conversion, or a settings difference. Fix the wrong path, re-run the 22-query parity, and switch chDB's default to Arrow if all 22 match.\n\nGuardrails: work in a linked worktree (make worktree-create); never edit the primary clone; heavy work only through make heavy-run; container checks under mocker one stack at a time (limits in tests/uat docs and the uat-mocker-compose-gaps-20261106 context); no live cloud without owner approval; no explanatory comments; changelog fragment if user-facing.",
